From 6b181e7a202eb50659ccbdc988491a552e5e92db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: apple: add opt-in A9 AOP observer and guarded sensor
 groundwork

Observe five fixed wrapper registers under existing PMGR domain locks without becoming a power consumer. Keep debug and attach-preflight parameters off by default; never access FIFO, IRQ, reset or remap controls. Refuse running ownership and stopped memory-contract gaps explicitly.

Isolate the old 56-bit RTKit codec and bounded SPU v2 protocol helpers. Add a dormant IIO consumer requiring verified calibration, units, ARot and a real first sample. No transport calls it until queue ownership and loading are established.
